# Turning a face-down creature face up is a special action (CR 116.2b, 701.40b), not an activated ability (CR 602.1), so
# Clarion Conqueror's "activated abilities of artifacts, creatures, and planeswalkers can't be activated" (CR 602.5) leaves
# it alone. On turn 1 Bot1 has Turn Inside Out and Lightning Bolt kill its Llanowar Elves, and manifest dread puts a second
# Llanowar Elves onto the battlefield face down. On turn 5 Bot1 casts the Conqueror, then turns the face-down creature face
# up for {G} from its Forest (the special action allowed). Face up, the Elves is a creature, and its mana ability is refused
# (an activated ability still stopped by the same card).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Turn Inside Out
Lightning Bolt
Plains
Llanowar Elves
Island
Plains
Clarion Conqueror
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

